<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU stability pact to help economy - Italy's Prodi.</title>
<headline>EU stability pact to help economy - Italy's Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi said on Friday that the EU's deal on a pact to enforce fiscal discipline after monetary union would help guarantee economic growth across the 15-nation bloc.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal was fair and sufficient for the future of European stability and growth,&quot; Prodi told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;It was not a compromise, it was an agreement. The market will like this,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Prodi said the accord struck the right balance between those who wanted a &quot;relaxed&quot; discipline and those seeking a &quot;rigid&quot; discipline.</p>
<p>&quot;This is not a victory for any one country, but for all of Europe. Everyone will leave this summit with a greater peace of mind about the possibility of the European Union working together,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
